cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Study 01, please cite this research artifact."
type: software
title: "Study 01: Negative-result validity in an OT/ICS cyber range"
authors:
  - family-names: Terayama
    given-names: Daichi
    alias: schutzz
repository-code: "https://github.com/schutzz/toyotamahime"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A public research and reproduction artifact for evaluating when a negative
  detection result from an OT/ICS cyber range is interpretable. Study 01
  includes the frozen protocol and apparatus, expected comparison targets,
  claims and limitations, a reproduction runbook, and provenance.
keywords:
  - cyber range
  - reproducibility
  - experimental validity
  - negative detection result
  - OT security
  - ICS security
version: 1.0.0
